  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ecological transition towards sustainable municipalities in Cuba</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of Energy Delivery Models, prioritizing the energy, agri-food and environmental sectors, with a focus on organizational innovation and digitalization. The project is implemented by UNDP in cooperation with local authorities. The project, which is funded by Norway, focuses on one of a total of nine municipalities that are part of a larger initiative between UNDP, the EU and Italy. The focus is twofold: food security and sustainable development. The funds are allocated to strengthening local distributors and producers of fruit &#x2013; mainly mango, papaya and guava. The project also finances solar-based technology that ensures the distribution and processing of fruit, as other sources of energy supply are highly inaccessible, and it serves as a pilot project in this regard. The objective of the project is to strengthen ties between local stakeholders, the private sector and the authorities, and to make a very important industry in Cuba more efficient through new technology.</narrative>
  </description>
